# Scripts below run inside Linux containers (Fly's Dockerfile, Render's
# build step). This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true,
# which normally checks these out as CRLF. A script starting
# "#!/usr/bin/env sh\r" fails at exec with "no such file or directory" -
# the Dockerfile already fixes the executable-bit half of this problem
# (chmod +x, since the bit itself doesn't survive a Windows checkout); this
# fixes the line-ending half. Force LF regardless of the checkout
# platform's autocrlf setting.
backend/bin/* text eol=lf
backend/build.sh text eol=lf

# Not a script, but the same class of problem: Cloudflare parses _redirects
# line by line. CI builds on Linux and is unaffected, so this only bites a
# manual `wrangler pages deploy dist` run from a Windows checkout - a failure
# that would show up as SPA routing silently not working, with no build error.
frontend/public/_redirects text eol=lf
